  "unit": "Unit 2 - Percent",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 2 - Percent for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p>A <strong>percent</strong> is a ratio out of 100.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mtext>Percent</mtext><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Part</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>Whole</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>100</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li>50% = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>  </li>\n<li>25% = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>  </li>\n<li>200% = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Formula</h3>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mtext>Percent&#x000A0;Change</mtext><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>New</mtext><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mtext>Original</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>Original</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>100</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Positive → increase  </li>\n<li>Negative → decrease  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Examples</strong><br />\n1. Price from \\<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>40</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>\\</mi></mrow></math>50:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi><mtext>&#x000A0;increase</mtext></mrow></math>\n\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Price from \\<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>80</mn><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>\\</mi></mrow></math>60:  </li>\n</ol>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>80</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi><mtext>&#x000A0;decrease</mtext></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Simple Interest</h3>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> = principal  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math> = rate (decimal)  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> = time  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: \\<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>I = 1000(0.05)(3)=150$  </p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Compound Interest</h3>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></math> = total  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> = principal  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math> = annual rate (decimal)  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></math> = times compounded per year  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> = time in years  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong>: \\$1000 at 5% compounded annually for 3 years  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1.05</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1157.63</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br />\n40% of students are girls. If there are 200 students, how many are girls?  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>200</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br />\nAn item is discounted 20%, then taxed 5%. If original price is \\$100:<br />\n- After discount: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></math><br />\n- After tax: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1.05</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>84</mn></mrow></math>  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Linear growth</strong>: constant <strong>addition</strong> per step<br />\n  Example: salary increases \\<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2000</mn><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>→</mi></mrow></math>y=2000t+P$  </li>\n<li><strong>Exponential growth</strong>: constant <strong>multiplication</strong> per step<br />\n  Example: bacteria doubles every hour → <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<p><strong>Linear growth/decay equation:</strong></p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: growth  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: decay  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br />\nA tank loses 5 liters per hour, starting with 200:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p><strong>General formula:</strong></p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>&#x000B1;</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x0002B;</mo></mrow></math> for growth  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo></mrow></math> for decay  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br />\nCar worth \\$20,000 depreciates 10% per year:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20000</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.9</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Positive association</strong>: as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> increases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math> tends to increase.  </li>\n<li><strong>Negative association</strong>: as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> increases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math> tends to decrease.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Examples</strong>\n- Hours studied vs. test score → positive<br />\n- Speed vs. travel time → negative  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) Convert: (a) 0.2 to percent, (b) 150% to decimal.<br />\n2) Find percent change: 60 → 45.<br />\n3) Simple interest: \\$800 at 6% for 2 years.<br />\n4) Compound interest: \\$500 at 8% annually for 2 years.<br />\n5) Linear growth: population starts at 1000, grows by 50 per year. Write equation.<br />\n6) Exponential decay: medicine amount starts at 200 mg, halves each hour. Write equation.<br />\n7) Identify association:<br />\n   - Number of hours worked vs. income.<br />\n   - Hours of TV watched vs. GPA.  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) (a) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi></mrow></math> (b) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>150</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow></math><br />\n2) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>100</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#x00025;</mi></mrow></math> (decrease)<br />\n3) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>800</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></math><br />\n4) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1.08</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>583.20</mn></mrow></math><br />\n5) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></math><br />\n6) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></math><br />\n7) Positive: hours worked vs. income. Negative: TV hours vs. GPA.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">\n</code></pre>",
